{"seq":19,"trial_id":"harness-zero-select-2026-11/zero-full-no-scoped-notes-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-03-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r4","wall_ts":"2026-11-05T22:22:18.356Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-16T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"d450139491635c03adbdf19383e506eece20edc675f9e78da41173a454944179","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I found three ticket numbers that are clearly Marrow Fieldworks, plus one that probably is:\n\n**Marrow Fieldworks tickets**\n- **PD-5302**: Hollis posted it in #central-random on Oct 14 (this week) as \"one more ticket number for Marrow Fieldworks,\" a follow-up from this week. He said no action is needed.\n- **#4409**: From Moss's note \"Central handoffs next week\" (Jan 2, 2026). It's a recurring timeout on the Gatehouse Check-In report at the Salina North yard (Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron, during the 06:00 flatbed intake).\n- **#4412**: From the same Moss note. It's a small glitch in the driver SMS prompt when combine trailers are staged on unpaved overflow lots.\n\n**Probably Marrow Fieldworks, but not named**\n- **#8841**: Tobias posted it in #central-random on Oct 13. It covers West yard Door 2 double-booking when flatbeds check in early. He called it \"Tobias's dealer account,\" not Marrow Fieldworks. The Moss note puts #4409 and #4412 on \"Pree's dealer account\" under the Fieldworks handoff, so #8841 is likely the same account after it changed hands. I can't confirm that, because I can't see the account files.\n\n**Similar names, left out**\n- **FR-882** (Moss note) and **PD-4821** (#central-team, June) are for Marrow Agrisupply.\n- **#88412** (#central-team) is for Tansleigh Packaging.\n\nMoss's other Central note, the cheat sheet, has no ticket numbers. Your other channels have no Marrow Fieldworks tickets from this week."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1792159200.000127"}}
